message.content:
Use CSS’s **`:hover`** pseudo-class; it works on a `span` because `:hover` can be applied to all elements, not just links.[6]

```html
<span class="hover-text">Hover me</span>
```

```css
.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If you want a smoother effect, you can add a transition:

```css
.hover-text {
  transition: color 0.2s ease;
}

.hover-text:hover {
  color: red;
}
```

If the `span` contains other elements or your color change is being overridden by more specific styles, you may need to increase specificity or use `!important` as a last resort.[1]

